{
  "slug": "grainulator",
  "name": "Grainulator",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Research sprint orchestrator for Claude Code. Ask a question, get a decision-ready brief — every finding is tracked as a typed claim, adversarially challenged, confidence-graded, and compiled into self-contained HTML output. Zero dependencies, MIT licensed.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **19 skills**, **1 agent**, **2 hooks** and **4 MCP servers**.\n\n- **Skills** (19): `blind-spot` (Structural gap analysis -- find what the sprint has not considered), `brief` (Generate a compiled decision brief from the current sprint's claims), `calibrate` (Score past predictions against actual outcomes), `challenge` (Adversarial testing of a specific claim), `feedback` (Record stakeholder input — new constraints, corrections, or direction changes), `fetch` (Size-efficient URL fetch with semantic extraction), `harvest` (Sprint analytics — type distributions, stale claims, velocity, prediction scoring), `healthcheck` (Fast pre-flight health check for all Grainulator MCP servers), and 11 more\n- **Agents** (1): `grainulator` (Autonomous research sprint subagent)\n- **Hooks** (2): `PostToolUse`, `PreToolUse`\n- **MCP servers** (4): `wheat`, `mill`, `silo`, `deepwiki`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install grainulator@claude-community` from `grainulation/grainulator`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 19,
    "agent": 1,
    "hook": 2,
    "mcp": 4
  },
